From 71f42b3a41294b0676a5dbaf04a013e1b1ee2348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:31:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 015/122] ATTRIB/ATTDEF: decode the R2018 embedded MTEXT of
 multi-line attributes

ODA 20.4.4: for mtext_type 2 or 4 "all fields of an embedded MTEXT
object are written, starting from the Entmode". As ACadSharp
readCommonAttData (readEntityMode + readMText without the common data),
and measured on AutoCAD's R2018 sample_AC1032.dwg (ATTDEF 796, ATTRIB
79D):

- the common entity part has the ownerhandle (if entmode 0, written as
  0), reactors, xdic, has_ds_data, a full ENC color (RGB before the
  transparency), and the flags in the order ltype, material, shadow,
  plotstyle (not as in the common entity data), with the LAYER, LTYPE,
  MATERIAL, PLOTSTYLE and visualstyle handles.
- the MTEXT has extents_height before extents_width, the bg fill
  fields with 0x10 too, and the R2018 annotation fields incl. the
  redundant ones and columns, as DWG_ENTITY (MTEXT).
- the STYLE handle of the ATTRIB/ATTDEF comes before the embedded MTEXT
  handles in the handle stream.
- after the MTEXT: annotative_data_size, and if > 0 the data, the
  registered application (annotative_style) and a BS (annotative_flag).

Before, the MTEXT layer pointed to the STYLE Standard and the ATTRIB
layer was wrong. Now the data stream ends exactly at the string stream
(@106.7 and @137.7) and all handles point to LAYER 0, LTYPE ByLayer,
MATERIAL ByLayer and STYLE Standard. dwgdiff against ACadSharp on the
22 acadsharp samples: value differences 10 -> 0, nothing else changed.

The fields are now written as mtext.<field> in JSON, which in_json
reads back into the embedded struct (before, flat keys like ins_pt
clashed with the ATTRIB fields). New struct fields ownerhandle,
reactors, xdicobjhandle, ltype, material, plotstyle and the 3
visualstyle handles (dynapi.c and dynapi.texi edited by hand,
gen-dynapi.pl needs Convert::Binary::C).

GEOPOSITIONMARKER uses the same macro and keeps its former trailing
is_really_locked and annotative data; it is unverified, no sample.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
